":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"xfY46Z-nBtX6sZQLxrdxhQ","review_id":"yDnZnayriuzVheQZrW9Byg","date":"2009-05-26T04:30:32","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9414188861846924,"text_excerpt":"Very cute and quiet place. My coworkers and I were looking for a place to have a non-fried dinner and ended up at Tommy's. The service was friendly and attentive. I was impressed with the quality of the wines by the glass as well. Any place that has La Crema and Cakebread by the glass is just fine by me. I was a little disappointed that they ran out of sugar cubes for my champagne cocktail, but they found a work around so it was all good. They start you off with some amazing bruschetta. For the first course, I had the escargot and it was amazing. The butter based sauce looked like it was going to be way too heavy, but it was surprisingly light and delicious. Also a very interesting prepar..."},{"business_id":"xfY46Z-nBtX6sZQLxrdxhQ","review_id":"ZwLqG4p3la8hYCygKubnbA","date":"2010-06-20T19:06:32","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.935657799243927,"text_excerpt":"My husband and I went to dinner on Friday night and fell in love with Tommy's. What a great restaurant. Our waiter David was excellent - we didn't have to wait for drinks, the atmosphere is romantic and the food is out of this world. We split a salad, oysters and a shrimp and pasta dish. All of it was excellent. We can't wait to go back. We didn't have a reservation and were able to walk right in and get a table - we did arrive early. It was around 6:30."},{"business_id":"xfY46Z-nBtX6sZQLxrdxhQ","review_id":"7g0cjXyyzBJKKiCHv6m5kw","date":"2011-12-23T04:10:14","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9321067333221436,"text_excerpt":"We went to Tommy's to celebrate my wife's birthday. As always, she wants a special dinner for her special day. After tossing around a few ideas and reading some reviews, Tommy's rose to the top of her list. We made the reservations. We were a little late, but they had held our table. No complaints from the hostess. The dining area is actually three different rooms, one of which is in the bar area. We sat in what I took to be the main dining area. Nice old style wooden decor with plenty of mirrors to give the appearance of a larger room. They have a nice wine list, not too badly priced for a downtown restaurant. One strange quirk... Each menu had a slightly different wine list. I ordered a..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"xfY46Z-nBtX6sZQLxrdxhQ","photo_id":"QAcuJPqTaO4S1WnT1YdylA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/QAcuJPqTaO4S1WnT1YdylA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8970578908920288},{"bus